    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of aniline is subjected to reaction with excess of acetic anhydride to prepare acetanilide. The mass of acetanilide produced if the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completed is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>.</p><p>(Given molar mass in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>"
  },
